{"id":1826227,"retrievedAt":"2026-11-15T17:50:17.657Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/ktNV17nNrDDav3HAN85aByDA1im.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[{"id":99,"name":"Documentary"},{"id":18,"name":"Drama"}],"homepage":"https://giloo.ist/zh-TW/episodes/2000","id":1826227,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["HK"],"original_language":"cn","original_title":"對話 shall we talk","overview":"Gemma is from Linyi, Shandong, and Sandra is from Taichung, Taiwan. They became good friends while studying in Hong Kong. During the 2019 Hong Kong anti-extradition bill movement, they interviewed eighteen friends from mainland China, Hong Kong, and Taiwan who held slightly different stances. Together, they explored how individuals think, act, and reflect on themselves amid a defining social movement of their era. Finally, they invited two actors to perform one dialogue and two monologues, addressing the unspoken words, suppressed empathy, and misunderstood remarks. How have we been shaped by social movements? Who have we grown closer to, and who have we drifted apart from? This rift makes us yearn for conversation. Years later, this social movement has not truly ended. Are you still having those conversations?","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/kgrJOqJa2KG5ahasVjMnQX8oNlS.jpg","production_companies":[{"id":318781,"logo_path":"/w45wI0NO9F7Hke2AECTg0wncVAN.png","name":"Keio University","origin_country":"JP"},{"id":318782,"logo_path":"/ou0iOH9OkISzrlqadxX5S2fcw2g.png","name":"Centre For Community Cultural Development","origin_country":"HK"}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"HK","name":"Hong Kong"},{"iso_3166_1":"JP","name":"Japan"}],"release_date":"2019-12-11","revenue":0,"runtime":22,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[{"english_name":"Cantonese","iso_639_1":"cn","name":"广州话 / 廣州話"}],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"Shall We Talk: A Dialogue","video":false,"vote_average":5,"vote_count":1,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[],"cre